Aston x Warwick Cybersecurity CTF

Overview

I participated in an inter-university Capture The Flag (CTF) competition hosted by Aston University and Warwick University student societies.
My team achieved 3rd place overall and was the only Aston University team to finish on the podium.


Challenge Areas

Digital Forensics
Investigated files and metadata to identify hidden information and recover challenge flags.

Steganography
Examined image and audio files for concealed data using file analysis techniques.

Cryptography
Analysed encoded and encrypted data and applied appropriate decoding methods.

OSINT
Used publicly available information to identify clues and solve investigative challenges.

Tools Used
grep
CyberChef
Linux command line
Metadata analysis
Audio analysis
Image inspection tools


What I Learned

Teamwork is Critical
Many challenges were solved through collaboration and sharing different approaches.

Methodical Investigation
Systematically analysing files and evidence was more effective than randomly trying tools.

Practical Cybersecurity
The competition demonstrated how concepts such as cryptography, steganography and forensics are applied in practice rather than just theory.

Outcome
3rd Place Overall
Only Aston University team on the podium
Practical experience in multiple cybersecurity domains